        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p>Before an antibody drug reaches its first patient, it has to pass a series of technical decisions: whether the molecule is developable, whether a process change altered it, how fast it clears in animals, whether it provokes anti-drug antibodies, and what starting dose is safe in humans.</p><p>Every one of those answers sits in a stack of records: assay tables, batch histories, animal studies, regulatory reviews. Specialists read them, argue over them and make the call. We wanted to know whether today&#8217;s AI agents can make those calls too.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" tabindex=\"-1\" type=\"email\" /><input class=\"button primary\" type=\"submit\" value=\"Subscribe\" /><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p>So we built TxBench&#8211;Antibody Development: 60 decisions taken from real development programs, covering the seven stages from picking a lead to choosing the first human dose. Each one hands an agent the records and asks for a decision, with the numbers behind it. Code checks every answer against a fixed key, so no model grades another model.</p><p>The decisions come from public sources: 41 patents, 11 regulatory reviews, four published studies, three trial protocols or registry entries and one public dataset. We tested 34 setups, each a model paired with a harness (the software the model works inside, such as Claude Code, Codex or Pi). Every setup attempted every decision three times, for 6,110 graded attempts.</p><p>These 60 decisions come from public, retrospective records. Benchmark performance is distinct from the judgment of a development team.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cH8v!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bedcb59-4b1f-4a11-86fb-71fb3ee74b30_3471x937.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"393\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!cH8v!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bedcb59-4b1f-4a11-86fb-71fb3ee74b30_3471x937.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 1. Every decision carries one label for its development stage, the source of its records, the kind of decision and the main evidence it rests on.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>At a glance</h2><ol><li><p>The best setup, Grok 4.7 on Grok Build, got 39.4% right.</p></li><li><p>The closer a decision got to patients, the harder it was: toxicology and first-dose decisions passed 13% of the time.</p></li><li><p>On one program taken through five stages in sequence, only Opus 5.5 reached the end, in one of five runs.</p></li></ol><h2>The leaderboard</h2><p><strong>The highest pass rate was 39.4%.</strong> Grok 4.7 on Grok Build topped the table, just ahead of Opus 5 on Claude Code (37.2%) and Sonnet 5.5 on Pi (36.7%). At the bottom, GPT-5.6 Luna on Codex got 2.8%.</p><p>The low ceiling isn&#8217;t because the decisions are impossible. 57 of the 60 were solved by at least one setup.</p><p>Cost did not track accuracy. GPT-6 Astra on Pi and Opus 5.5 on Claude Code passed the same share of attempts (32.8%), at $0.46 and $3.47 per attempt.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!QCqp!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F872831d1-fc43-4934-936f-93018eab7fde_2521x1642.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"948\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!QCqp!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F872831d1-fc43-4934-936f-93018eab7fde_2521x1642.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 2. Pass rate for each of the 34 model&#8211;harness setups, alongside mean cost, tokens, wall-clock time and tool calls per run. Colors identify the model&#8217;s lab; marker shapes identify the harness.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>The closer the development stage gets to patients the harder it gets</h2><p><strong>Toxicology and first-dose decisions passed 13% of the time.</strong> Averaged over all setups, that compares with 31% for glycosylation and quality control and 33% for immunogenicity.</p><p>No model led every stage. Gemini 4 Argon passed 87% of the manufacturing decisions but none of the first-dose decisions. Grok 4.7 was the reverse: none of the manufacturing decisions, but two thirds of the first-dose decisions. Opus 5.5 was the only model to pass a cytokine-release safety margin, the calculation that keeps a first dose below the level that triggers a dangerous immune reaction.</p><ul><li><p><strong>39.4%</strong>: the highest pass rate of any setup</p></li><li><p><strong>57 of 60</strong>: decisions that at least one setup solved</p></li><li><p><strong>13%</strong>: the average pass rate on toxicology and on first-dose decisions</p></li></ul><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"255\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!52nu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F84b24d07-42f7-47a5-a436-c4d3981222c7_2556x448.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div></div></div></div><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 3. Pass rate across the seven development stages, with one flagship model from each lab in color and the other models in gray.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p8XF!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e14a0b9-1cac-4b39-841f-dd806b255a6a_1450x940.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"940\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!p8XF!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0e14a0b9-1cac-4b39-841f-dd806b255a6a_1450x940.png\" width=\"1450\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 4. Pass rates by decision type, evidence source and failure class across 21 models. Outlined cells mark the leader in each column.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FIk5!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F04dafddc-612d-4ba4-9651-6c8df23ca66f_700x284.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"284\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!FIk5!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F04dafddc-612d-4ba4-9651-6c8df23ca66f_700x284.png\" width=\"700\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 5. Mean pass rate across the six failure classes, separating the computational class from the interpretive classes.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>Combining 5 stages of a development program</h2><p>Development decisions depend on each other, so we also built one program that runs through five stages in sequence, separate from the 60. An agent takes four candidate antibodies through developability, mouse pharmacokinetics, immunogenicity, safety and nomination, and the first human dose, building on its own earlier answers at each step.</p><p><strong>Only Opus 5.5 reached the end, in one of five runs.</strong> Grok 4.7 and GPT-6 Astra failed the first step in every run, and Gemini 4 Argon got past it once.</p><p>In the mouse study, one candidate&#8217;s first blood sample was unusually low. Opus 5.5 read it as a dosing artifact rather than fast clearance in 13 of 13 runs; the other models did so in 0 of 36. This let Opus 5.5 pass the safety and nomination step in two runs, a step no model passed when it was given on its own.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!udC2!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F25655931-b84c-4003-95af-54fe1e4089e2_2515x1718.png\" target=\"_blank\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><source type=\"image/webp\" /><img alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\" height=\"995\" src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!udC2!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F25655931-b84c-4003-95af-54fe1e4089e2_2515x1718.png\" width=\"1456\" /><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"><svg class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\" fill=\"none\" height=\"20\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"20\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">Figure 6. The five development reviews, the share of runs still on track after each review, and model performance on each review within the chain and on its own.</figcaption></figure></div><h2>Resources</h2><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://benchmarks.bio/txbench-abdev\">Leaderboard and example evaluations</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://latch.bio/txbench-ab-dev\">Manuscript</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://github.com/latchbio/antibody-discovery-internal\">GitHub</a></p></li></ul><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" tabindex=\"-1\" type=\"email\" /><input class=\"button primary\" type=\"submit\" value=\"Subscribe\" /><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>"
